meta {
  name: Delete Node
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

delete {
  url: {{serveUrl}}/config/nodes/{{nodeName}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Removes the node {{nodeName}} from the config served by `realm serve`.

  A whole new config is instanced without the node before replacing the
  current one, so it is rejected while loads or jobs still reference it.

  After the change, the cluster state is planned on the state file and, if
  the cluster is running, rolled out to it. The response `cluster` field
  holds the planned diff (`plan`), whether the cluster runs it (`updated`)
  and why planning or updating failed (`error`); the config change is kept
  even if they fail.

  Responses: 200 deleted, 404 node not found, 409 the config without the
  node is invalid (e.g. loads or jobs reference it).
  Body: {"cluster": {...}}
}
